Парафраз из великих.

XMLgen - The simplest? XML generator, MIT (c) 2026 miktim@mail.ru

The jar ./dist/xmlgen-... file was generated with debugging info using JDK1.8 for target JRE1.7

package org.miktim.xmlgen;

class XML extends Node;
  Constructor:
    XML();
      - returns empty root node.
  Methods:
    String toString();
      - returns XML text with declaration: <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>.

class Node;
    Node is XML element node.
  Constructors:
    Node();
      - returns "null" node. Doesn't generate anything.
    Node(String tag);
      - the tag is a node name with an optional prefix and optional attributes;
      - let me remind you that there should be no spaces in names.
        For example:
          new Node("prop xmlns:R=\"http://ns.example.com/schema/\"");
          new Node("R:author", "John Doe").
    Node(String tag, Object content);
      - the content of the String type are escaped;
      - the content can be null. Generates <tag/>
  Methods:
    Node setNode(Node node);
      - adds node to the current node;
      - returns node.
    Node addNode(Node node);
      - adds node to the current node;
      - returns current node.
    Node setNode(String tag);
      - adds new node to the current node;
      - returns new node.
    Node addNode(String tag);
      - adds new node to the current node;
      - returns current node.
    Node setNode(String tag, Object content);
      - adds new node to the current node;
      - returns new node.
    Node addNode(String tag, Object content);
      - adds new node to the current node;
      - returns current node.
    
    boolean isEmpty();
      - checks if the node (xml) is empty.
    static String escape(String value);
      - escapes "<", ">", "&".
    String toString();
      - returns XML text as a single line.

Example:

  XML xml = new XML();
  xml.setNode("multistatus xmlns=\"DAV:\"")
    .setNode("response")
    .addNode("href", "http://www.example.com/container/")
    .setNode("propstat")
    .addNode("status", "HTTP/1.1 200 OK")
    .setNode("prop xmlns:R=\"http://ns.example.com/schema/\"")
    .addNode("R:author", "John Doe")
    .addNode("creationdate", "2026-06-12T23:20:50.52Z")
    .addNode("displayname", "container")
    .addNode("supportedlock", null);

xml.toString() returns following XML text (actually as single line):

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<multistatus xmlns="DAV:">
  <response>
    <href>http://www.example.com/container/</href>
    <propstat>
      <status>HTTP/1.1 200 OK</status>
      <prop xmlns:R="http://ns.example.com/schema/">
        <R:author>John Doe</R:author>
        <creationdate>2026-06-12T23:20:50.52Z</creationdate>
        <displayname>container</displayname>
        <supportedlock/>
      </prop>
    </propstat>
  </response>
</multistatus>
